{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"edacious-exoteric-cowrie","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Target\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py` — **800 LOC** on origin/main against the 800-LOC hard cap (0 lines of headroom).\n\nThis file is AT the cap. Any edit at all currently fails CI.\n\n## How to do it\nRead the file and derive the seam from the CALL GRAPH — do not take any hint above as the answer.\nExtract a cluster of functions that already call each other and that share one concern. The commit\nmessage must NAME the concern boundary you chose and why the call graph supports it.\n\n## Constraints (inherited from the epic — all non-negotiable)\n- Split along LOGICAL CONCERNS / ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARIES, never mechanically to hit a number.\n- NEVER raise the limit; `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is locked.\n- No resulting file under 100 LOC; target 200-500 LOC each.\n- Leave REAL headroom — landing at 798 recreates the problem (that is how Gerrit 1916 failed).\n- Behaviour-preserving: existing tests for this area must pass UNMODIFIED. If a test must change,\n  the split was not behaviour-preserving — stop and reconsider the seam.\n- Serena `find_referencing_symbols` for references, THEN `grep` for each moved symbol AS A STRING\n  (monkeypatch.setattr / getattr / importlib). Serena returns EMPTY, not an error, for `Any`\n  receivers, so the grep is mandatory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py` is under the cap with real headroom, and every new file is >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] The split follows an existing call-graph seam; the commit message names the concern boundary.\n- [ ] Behaviour unchanged: existing tests covering this area pass UNMODIFIED.\n- [ ] The CI module-size gate passes without touching `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the complexity ratchet shows no new or increased entries.\n- [ ] All references updated — verified by BOTH a semantic reference search AND a string grep.","id":"4af3-793e-6b34-4290","parent_id":"2490-cb4b-29ac-4c7c","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Split _engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py (800 LOC) along its concern boundary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788219293505597001,"uuid":"66e3b22e-f278-49bf-9791-fb9192c988de"}